  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/svg/fire.svg",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p>This Spell can be cast and held as a swirling ring of fire around your ring finger until you unleash it. Only one ring may be held at a time. The next time you perform an Attack Action, it must be this Spell (at no additional Mana cost). If anyone touches the ring with the intent to diffuse it (you may oppose that Action), the Attack hits them for half damage. The appendage they touched you with smolders, useless for a number of rounds equal to the damage inflicted.</p><p>The target gains the Burned Debuff.</p><p><em>The \"charge and hold, release on next Attack\" mechanic and the interrupt/diffuse sub-mechanic have no structural support in this system - only the eventual damage roll is represented mechanically; apply the rest by hand.</em></p>",
